<title>USA: Ryder hires IBM, Andersen in $1.4 bln deal.</title>
<headline>Ryder hires IBM, Andersen in $1.4 bln deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp and Andersen Consulting said that they are teaming up to manage Ryder System Inc's technology and telecommunications operations in a deal worth almost $1.4 billion over 10 years.</p>
<p>IBM's Global Services business and Andersen said under Ryder's leadership, they will develop a new logistics system and improve the computer systems Ryder already has in place.</p>
<p>The two companies will also take over and manage Ryder's company-wide technology and telecommunications operations. As a result, Ryder said it will save $160 million over 10 years.</p>
</text>
